-- Every support section (`Requires:`, `Enables:`, and all `Appendix:` entries:
-- documentation items, mapping `writing:`/`as:`, `justification:`, `aliases:`,
-- item-level `writing:`, `references:`, and `metadata:`).


-- Mapping-rendering templates (`writing:`/`as:`) and full documentation fields
-- directly inside `Appendix:`.
[\real.sequence]
Declares: X ::= x(i_) is \function:on{\naturals.set}:to{\reals.set}
Appendix:
. called: "real sequence"
. written: "\{x_n\}"
. writing: x(i)
  as: "x?_{i?}"
. writing: x(i_)
  as: "\left(x?_{i_?}\right)_{i_?=0}^{\infty}"
. overview: "An infinite sequence of real numbers indexed by the natural
             numbers."
. description: "A real sequence assigns a real value to each natural-number
                index."
. related: "#algebra"
. discoverer: "@emmy.noether"
Id: "0b81f148-f5c4-411d-bbaa-6f5dd4566db6"


-- `Requires:` states what a *use* of the command must establish beforehand:
-- a `capability:` provides a spec operator, and a `definition:` requires a
-- named `Defines:` command to establish a fact.
[\pointed.natural.set]
Declares: X
Requires:
. capability: x_ "in" X :-> \\abstract
. definition: \zero is \natural
Appendix:
. called: "pointed set over the naturals"
Id: "b4643f0c-2a8e-4b8c-9c45-daf810276e37"


-- `Enables:` states what knowing the type allows downstream: capabilities,
-- `from:` coerced-literal capabilities, and `view:` conversions.
[\carrier.magma]
Declares: G ::= (X, *) is \set via X
specifies: * is \operation:on{G}
Enables:
. capability: x_ "in" G :-> x_ is \element:of{X}
  written: "x_? \in G?"
. from: Y ::= {y__ : ...}
  capability: x_ "in" G :-> x_ memberOf Y
. view:
  as: S := X is \set
Appendix:
. called: "magma with carrier element capability"
Id: "80bdeb53-b07a-411c-b7e2-7bd81e2059cb"


-- `Appendix:` `. justification:` holds labeled `have:` groups. A `[:label:]`
-- on a specification or clause points at a matching `for: (:label:)` entry.
[\product.pair.set]
Declares: P ::= (A, B)
specifies:
. A is \set
. (.B is \set.)[:second_factor:]
Appendix:
. called: "ordered pair of sets"
. justification:
  . for: (:second_factor:)
    have: B is \set
    asserting: B is \set
    because: "Both factors of the pair are assumed to be sets."
Id: "decbcbc2-aa62-430f-aa16-d044ea928c10"


-- `Appendix:` `. aliases:`, item-local `. writing:`, `. references:` (both
-- item-wide `$resource` and label-specific `. for:`/`. entry:`), and
-- `. metadata:` `. version:`.
[\squaring.magma]
Declares: G ::= (X, *) is \set via X
specifies: * is \operation:on{X}
satisfies:
. [closure]
  forAll: x "in" X
  then: x * x "in"? X
Appendix:
. called: "magma with squaring notation"
. aliases:
  . alias: square(x_) :=> x_ * x_
    written: "x_?^{2}"
. writing:
  . "carrier :~> \mathrm{carrier}"
. references:
  . $bourbaki.algebra
  . for: (:closure:)
    entry: $bourbaki.algebra:page{12}
. metadata:
  . version: "1.0"
Id: "9b8fdb86-1a09-4859-83ac-dc03c3d46fd2"


-- The `Enables:` capability on `\carrier.magma` reduces a membership spec fact
-- `y "in" G` to the type fact `y is \element:of{X}`.
Theorem:
given:
. G ::= (X, *) is \carrier.magma
. y "in" G
then: y is? \element:of{X}
Appendix:
. called: "an enabled capability reduces magma membership to carrier elements"
Id: "6f2caf05-a403-49ae-9ffd-28530e77efec"
